{
 "task": "Make a vertical animated cartoon short of MY story, built in code: three.js r160 world + canvas-drawn 2D character cards, rendered frame by frame in headless Chromium (Playwright, swiftshader), encoded with ffmpeg. 1080x1920, 30fps, exactly as long as my voiceover. Work start to finish; only ask if script and audio don't match.",
 "my_inputs": {
  "story": "[your idea, true event, legend or full script]",
  "script": "[optional exact script]",
  "voiceover": "[optional: attach mp3/wav]",
  "length_seconds": 30,
  "voice_speed": 1.0,
  "captions": false,
  "notes": "[optional: era, setting, characters, jokes]"
 },
 "stages": [
  "A. No script: write one at ~3.7 words/s (30s~110 words): 1) hook = absurd fact, no setup 2) setting in 1-2 lines with a concrete detail 3) 2-4 escalating beats, others doubt/mock, one exaggeration joke 4) pivot 'But...'/'You see,' revealing the real mechanism with an everyday analogy 5) short ironic twist = last words. Spoken English, contractions, numbers as words, never describe what's on screen. If presented as true, web-check facts and say history/disputed/legend.",
  "B. No voiceover: give script in a copyable block + word count + est. length, a short shot plan, recording tips (one warm narrator; ElevenLabs speed 1.05-1.1, stability 45-55%; pauses at sentence ends; no music). Stop and ask for the upload.",
  "C. With voiceover: build everything below without stopping. Task list for progress; send a stills contact sheet before the long render."
 ],
 "setup": [
  "mkdir -p web/lib work stills frames out",
  "npm pack three@0.160.0 -> copy package/build/three.module.js to web/lib (fallback: sparse git clone of mrdoob/three.js branch r160, folder build)",
  "Playwright + Chromium (npm i -g playwright && npx playwright install chromium); launch args --use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader --ignore-gpu-blocklist",
  "python3 numpy Pillow, ffmpeg (with rubberband)",
  "Serve web/ with a tiny Node http server; render.mjs loads index.html, waits for window.ready, calls window.renderFrame(f), saves canvas.toDataURL('image/jpeg',.95) to frames/f0000.jpg. Support RESUME=1 (skip existing) and a frame list 'a-b' or '1,5,9'."
 ],
 "timing": "If voice_speed!=1: ffmpeg -af rubberband=tempo=<speed> (pitch kept). Claude can't hear audio: align my script to speech using ffmpeg silencedetect (-35dB, 0.12s): split script into phrases at punctuation, DP-match phrases to speech segments by syllable count vs duration, penalise sentence ends inside a segment. Spread words by syllables. Write work/phrases.json; check pauses fall at sentence ends. Frames = round(duration*30). Every reaction lands 0-3 frames before its word; the final payoff lands on the final word.",
 "architecture": {
  "files": "web/index.html (canvas#c 1080x1920 + module main.js), main.js (renderer, materials, world, cards, sprites, passes), story.js (SHOTS, LIGHTS, lightFor, camAt, dofAt, worldAt, actorsAt, fxAt: all pure functions of frame f), motion.js, paint.js (canvas textures), toon.js (character + creature drawing), audio.py, mix.py, finish.sh, sheet.py (contact sheets).",
  "renderer": "WebGLRenderer antialias:false, preserveDrawingBuffer, PCFSoft shadows 2048, sun = DirectionalLight from az/el per light preset, shadow camera centred on each shot's action (ext 8-60m), HemisphereLight, Fog(colour = sky horizon). Camera Perspective, near .08 far 1500.",
  "materials": "MeshToonMaterial with a 2-texel gradientMap [90,255] Nearest = hard 2-step toon shading. Textures are CanvasTextures painted in code: flat base + soft blotches + dark seams/strokes, repeat-wrapped, colorSpace sRGB. Boxes use world-scaled UVs (constant texel density).",
  "passes": [
   "1 colour: render scene to HalfFloat RT (samples 4).",
   "2 normal+depth: swap every mesh material to a ShaderMaterial writing vec4(normal*.5+.5, viewDepth) (handle USE_INSTANCING: pos=instanceMatrix*pos). Cards/sprites write rgb 0 + depth with alpha-test (so they block but are never outlined). Hide sky, clouds, blob shadows. Fog and shadows off for this pass.",
   "3 ink+grade fullscreen: 16 taps on a ring of radius 2.5px*clamp(7/depth,.62,1.25); edge = smoothstep(.006,.02,(dS-d)/d) on the NEAR side of depth jumps only; crease = smoothstep(.88,.72,dot(n,nS))*.9 when depths are within 6%; skip card samples; sky counts as depth 1e4; fade ink 140-520m. colour = mix(c, #030203, e); saturation 1.08-1.15; gain/lift tint; vignette .2-.34; white flash uniform.",
   "4 lens: per-pixel CoC = cinf*(1-focus/d) (near side capped 1.4x); 48-tap golden-angle disc, each tap weighted by its own CoC so sharp foreground never bleeds; skip when cinf<.5. Output linearToOutputTexel."
  ],
  "sky": "inverted sphere following camera: mix(horizon, top, pow(y,.55)) + optional sun disc. Painted cloud billboards far away (650-900m), fog off, facing camera."
 },
 "characters": {
  "card": "Each character is a 1200x2000 CanvasTexture on a 1.35x2.25m plane with origin at the soles (design space 600x1000, soles at y=975, 1 design unit = 2.25mm). MeshBasicMaterial alphaTest .02, DoubleSide; shadow via customDepthMaterial with the same map (alphaTest .5); soft dark radial blob under the feet. Billboard on yaw only: rotY = atan2(cam.x-x, cam.z-z). Redraw a card only when its key (JSON of q()-rounded pose values) changes.",
  "proportions": "Bean body: head blob ~236 wide, legs 1.38xHH, torso 1.08xHH (stout 1.12), eyes ~1.47m high. Head = superellipse blob with slight egg + per-seed asymmetry. Torso = egg blob with a tunic skirt below. Legs/arms = thin curved strokes (5.8u/5.2u, u=headWidth/100) in a darker shade of the outfit; round dot hands; small boots.",
  "ink": "Outline colour #241726 (plum), width 5u, thicker on the side away from the light (light from upper-left, -120deg). Fills: base colour with a soft shadow gradient toward lower-right. Skin default #ffe2c2, also #f5c9a0 #ecd0b6 #c99067.",
  "faces": "Eyes 13u apart either side of centre. Kinds: dot, lid (half-closed), happy (arc), squeeze, shock (big white + small pupil + raised arc brows), slit, dash. Mouths: dash, frown, smirk, smile, grin (open with teeth line), laugh, o, O, wave (nervous), teeth. Brows are short tapered strokes; angle sets mood. Expressions: neutral, stern, grin, laugh, nervous (+sweat drop), shock, smile, pained, squint, smug/side-eye (half lids, pupils to one side). Blinks every 1.3-2.3s for 4 frames.",
  "outfits": "Built from parts: tunic colour, belt, buttons, pockets, sash, hat (slouch hat, cap, top hat, bonnet, helmet, crown, hair), beard/moustache, apron, dress, props in hands. Design new outfits for each story in the same flat style.",
  "arm_poses": "hang, point (+finger), up, wave, hip, belly, cheek (both = shock), salute (flat hand at brim, drawn over the head), thumb (thumbs-up), shrug, reach, lift, cross, prop-holding (pen, stamp, wrench, spear, sign). Whole upper body tilts about the hip; head tilts separately.",
  "creatures": "Animals are side-view canvas sprites (600x800 design, feet at y=780) on shared textures cached by pose key, so flocks of 50+ cost little: shaggy shaded body blob with fringe strokes, thick inked limbs, small head, big googly white eye with pupil that can look/side-eye, simple beak/snout. Legs via 2-bone IK with joint bent backward; run cycle 16 phases (foot x = hip + stride*cos, lift = max(0,sin)); poses: stand, run, peck/graze, smug. Flip the sprite when travel direction dot camera-right < 0."
 },
 "world": {
  "build": "Primitives only: boxes, cylinders, cones, squashed spheres, extrusions; group set-pieces with pivots driven by 0..1 progress from worldAt(f) with eased, staggered parts. Instanced meshes for crops/grass/rocks; clear a patch where the action happens.",
  "background": "low half-buried hill spheres, distant mesas or mountains (cone + snow cap), trees (trunk cylinder + 4-6 squashed sphere canopies), far houses, fog to the horizon colour.",
  "secondary_motion": "windmills turn, flags/cloth wave (vertex sine), smoke/dust/leaves/Zzz/stars as cached 2D fx sprites, water shader scroll, wheels roll with distance/radius, vehicles bounce.",
  "text": "Diegetic text (signs, crates, letters, stamps) painted on canvas with real fonts; place on +z faces or planes so it never reads mirrored. Swap textures to animate (e.g. stamp appears on impact)."
 },
 "lights": {
  "day": "sun az64 el50 #fff3df 2.45, hemi sky #d2e2f6 ground #a8905e 1.1, sky top #2d74d4 horizon #cfe3f5, fog 120-1300, sat 1.12, vig .2",
  "golden": "sun az30 el11 #ffb46a 2.9, hemi #a99bcc/#7a5040 .98, sky #6474c0 -> #ffc485 + sun disc, gain #fff0e0, sat 1.15, vig .26, tint cards #ffe2c4",
  "dusk": "sun el5 #ff9a72 .9, hemi #5d6cab/#3a3048 .8, sky #18234f -> #d18a7c, gain #e2e8ff, lift #04050b, vig .34, a warm point-light lamp, tint cards #c9cff2",
  "use": "day = normal story, golden = decline or time passing, dusk-blue = explanation or ending. Time jump = 6-frame white flash."
 },
 "motion": {
  "helpers": "smooth(t)=t^3(t(6t-15)+10); easeOut=1-(1-t)^3; back(t)=overshoot s=1.7; spring settle; Catmull-Rom spline through via-points; idle(f,seed)={bob .006 sin(.11f), tilt 1.2deg sin(.05f), headTilt 1.5deg sin(.037f)}; blinkAt(f,seed); q(x)=round for card keys.",
  "camera": "Keys {f,pos,look,fov,roll,ease,path} inside cut-free segments; glides 18-45 frames; easeOut for whips/reveals; every hold creeps (fov *= 1-.00012*(f-f0)); 3-5deg roll on drama; impact kick = 7-frame alternating look offset + roll that decays. Vehicles: track alongside, match speed, slight judder.",
  "continuity": "prefer one continuous move: MCU pull-back into a wide, crane up and over a fence into the establishing shot, lateral truck along a lineup, crane down into an insert, rack focus to the background gag. Hard cut only on place/time jumps.",
  "acting": "anticipation -> back overshoot -> spring settle; pop-ins scale 0->1 with back easing + dust puff; stamp = 2-frame dip + puff + kick; laughs = alternating tilt + bob; head bobs on stressed words; nothing static for 4+ frames.",
  "walks_runs": "feet planted, bob 3-7%; run phase = speed/stride; fast movers must stay in frame until their beat is done."
 },
 "shot_grammar": {
  "plan_first": "work/PLAN.md: one row per shot (frames, words, setting, light, camera, cast/poses/expressions, fx, sfx). Usually one shot per phrase; merge tiny ones. Illustrate every sentence literally; props carry the jokes.",
  "order": "frame 0 = hook MCU of the hero mid-action -> pull-back reveal on the punch of sentence 1 -> wide establishing crane -> lineup/two-shot with pop-ins on each listed item -> reaction close-up (a creature or extra slides in with a side-eye on the question line) -> action wide (chase, scatter, collapse) -> time-jump flash -> insert on the key object -> twist: music stops, low sting, push-in with roll, payoff on the last word.",
  "framing": "Bean cards 2.25m tall: MCU = camera ~3.5m away at fov 32-34 looking at 1.35m; wides fov 40-52. Vertical frame half-width = d*tan(hfov/2), hfov = 2*atan(tan(vfov/2)*.5625): at 4m and fov 40 only +/-0.8m, so stage people in depth.",
  "lens": "DOF on close-ups/mediums (cInf 7-14, focus on the eyes), wides sharp, racks ~14 frames."
 },
 "audio": {
  "stems": "audio.py writes only music.wav + sfx.wav (48k mono, numpy synth). Music: short loop in the story's mood (march: kick/snare, plucked bass, brass pad, little fanfare; or plucky comedy; or eerie pad); stops on the twist line, then a low drone. SFX in frames/30: whoosh (low-passed noise with sine^2 envelope) on big moves, thunk (pitched sine drop + noise) on pops/stamps, rustle/leaves, feet patter, engine (pulse train low-passed), scrape, ting (2-4 kHz bells), sting (41 Hz + noise hit + brass stab) on the twist.",
  "mix": "mix.py: gated RMS of the voice (0.4s blocks above -40dB of max); scale music so its gated RMS = 0.5x voice (-6 dB); SFX = min(0.5x voice RMS, peaks 0.7x voice peak); sum; one linear gain only. No ducking, no compression. Print the measured levels and confirm.",
  "finish": "measure integrated loudness (ffmpeg ebur128), apply one volume gain to -14 LUFS + alimiter -1 dBFS; encode: ffmpeg -framerate 30 -i frames/f%04d.jpg -i mix.wav -c:v libx264 -preset slow -crf 17 -pix_fmt yuv420p -c:a aac -b:a 192k -shortest -movflags +faststart. QA: freezedetect (n=.0005, d=.4) and blackdetect must find nothing; make a 2fps tiled QA sheet and look at it."
 },
 "look_check": "Before the full render, render stills at every shot's middle plus key actions, tile them into a contact sheet, look at it and fix: cropped heads/hats, characters hidden by props or crops, camera inside objects, fast movers already out of frame, mirrored text, missing ink, empty frames. Send me the sheet, then render all frames in the background (about 3-6 s/frame on CPU), lock picture before sound.",
 "code_core": {
  "ink_shader_glsl": "uniform sampler2D col, nd; uniform vec2 res; uniform float px, sat, vig, flash; uniform vec3 fogCol, lift, gain; varying vec2 vUv;
float edgeAt(vec2 uv, float r){
vec4 c = texture2D(nd, uv); if (dot(c.rgb,c.rgb) < .01) return 0.; float d = c.a; vec3 n = c.rgb*2.-1.;
float e = 0.; float rr = r * clamp(7./d, .62, 1.25);
for (int i=0;i<16;i++){ float a = float(i)*.785398 + (i>7 ? .39 : 0.); float k = i>7 ? .5 : 1.;
vec2 o = vec2(cos(a), sin(a))*rr*k/res; vec4 s = texture2D(nd, uv+o);
float ds = s.a; bool card = dot(s.rgb,s.rgb) < .01;
if (card && ds > 0.) continue; // character cards: never outlined by the world ink
if (card) ds = 1e4; // sky
vec3 ns = s.rgb*2.-1.;
e = max(e, smoothstep(.006, .02, (ds - d)/d)); // depth jump, near side only
if (!card && abs(ds-d)/d < .06) e = max(e, smoothstep(.88, .72, dot(n, ns)) * .9); // crease
}
return e * (1. - smoothstep(140., 520., d)*.8);
}
void main(){
vec3 c = texture2D(col, vUv).rgb;
float e = edgeAt(vUv, px);
c = mix(c, vec3(.012,.01,.014), e);
if (flash < -0.5) c = vec3(e);
float l = dot(c, vec3(.299,.587,.114)); c = mix(vec3(l), c, sat);
c = c*gain + lift;
vec2 q = vUv-.5; c *= 1. - vig*dot(q*vec2(1.,.75), q*vec2(1.,.75))*2.2;
c = mix(c, vec3(1.), flash);
gl_FragColor = vec4(c,1.); }",
  "dof_shader_glsl": "uniform sampler2D src, nd; uniform vec2 res; uniform float focus, cinf, near; varying vec2 vUv;
float coc(vec2 uv){ float d = texture2D(nd, uv).a; if (d <= 0.) d = 2000.; float k = 1. - focus/d; return k > 0. ? cinf*k : min(-k*cinf*near, cinf*1.4); }
void main(){
float c0 = coc(vUv);
if (cinf < .5 || c0 < .6) { gl_FragColor = linearToOutputTexel(vec4(texture2D(src, vUv).rgb, 1.)); return; }
vec3 acc = vec3(0.); float wsum = 0.;
for (int i=0;i<48;i++){ float fi = float(i); float r = sqrt((fi+.5)/48.); float a = fi*2.39996;
vec2 o = vec2(cos(a), sin(a))*r*c0/res; float cs = coc(vUv+o);
float w = smoothstep(r*c0-1.5, r*c0+.5, cs + .5);
acc += texture2D(src, vUv+o).rgb*w; wsum += w; }
gl_FragColor = linearToOutputTexel(vec4(acc/max(wsum,1e-3), 1.)); }",
  "motion_js": "export const clamp = (x, a = 0, b = 1) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, x));
export const lerp = (a, b, t) => a + (b - a) * t;
export const lerp3 = (a, b, t) => a.map((v, i) => lerp(v, b[i], t));
export const ramp = (f, a, b) => clamp((f - a) / (b - a));
export const M = {
smooth: (t) => { t = clamp(t); return t * t * t * (t * (t * 6 - 15) + 10); }, 
easeOut: (t) => 1 - Math.pow(1 - clamp(t), 3), 
easeIn: (t) => Math.pow(clamp(t), 3),
back: (t, s = 1.7) => { t = clamp(t) - 1; return t * t * ((s + 1) * t + s) + 1; }, 
anticip: (t, s = 0.12) => { t = clamp(t); return t < 0.25 ? -s * Math.sin(t / 0.25 * Math.PI) : M.back((t - 0.25) / 0.75); }, 
spring: (t, freq = 3, damp = 5) => { t = Math.max(0, t); return 1 - Math.exp(-damp * t) * Math.cos(freq * 2 * Math.PI * t); }, 
};
export const spline = (pts, u) => {
const n = pts.length - 1, x = clamp(u) * n, i = Math.min(n - 1, Math.floor(x)), t = x - i;
const p0 = pts[Math.max(0, i - 1)], p1 = pts[i], p2 = pts[i + 1], p3 = pts[Math.min(n, i + 2)];
return p1.map((_, k) => 0.5 * ((2 * p1[k]) + (-p0[k] + p2[k]) * t + (2 * p0[k] - 5 * p1[k] + 4 * p2[k] - p3[k]) * t * t + (-p0[k] + 3 * p1[k] - 3 * p2[k] + p3[k]) * t * t * t));
};
export const camFromKeys = (K, f, { creep = 0.0012, kicks = [] } = {}) => {
let c;
if (f <= K[0].f) c = { ...K[0] };
else if (f >= K[K.length - 1].f) c = { ...K[K.length - 1] };
else {
const i = K.findIndex((k, j) => f >= k.f && f <= K[j + 1].f), a = K[i], b = K[i + 1];
const ease = M[b.ease || 'smooth'], t = ease((f - a.f) / (b.f - a.f));
if (b.path) { 
const pts = [a.pos, ...b.path, b.pos]; c = { pos: spline(pts, t), look: lerp3(a.look, b.look, t), fov: lerp(a.fov, b.fov, t), roll: lerp(a.roll || 0, b.roll || 0, t) };
} else c = { pos: lerp3(a.pos, b.pos, t), look: lerp3(a.look, b.look, t), fov: lerp(a.fov, b.fov, t), roll: lerp(a.roll || 0, b.roll || 0, t) };
}
c.fov *= 1 - creep * Math.max(0, f - K[0].f) * 0.15; 
for (const k of kicks) { const d = f - k.f; if (d >= 0 && d < 7) { const s = (d % 2 ? -1 : 1) * k.a * (1 - d / 7); c.look = [c.look[0], c.look[1] + s * 3, c.look[2] + s * 2]; c.roll = (c.roll || 0) + s * 20; } }
return c;
};
export const idle = (f, seed = 1) => ({
bob: 0.006 * Math.sin((f + seed * 11) * 0.11),
tilt: 1.2 * Math.sin((f + seed * 7) * 0.05),
headTilt: 1.5 * Math.sin((f + seed * 5) * 0.037 + 1),
});
export const blinkAt = (f, seed) => { const per = 38 + (seed * 17) % 31, ph = (f + seed * 13) % per; return ph < 2 ? 0.5 : ph < 4 ? 1 : 0; };
export const walk = (f, f0, speed = 1.1, stride = 0.8) => { const t = Math.max(0, f - f0) / 30; return { dist: t * speed, phase: (t * speed / (2 * stride)) % 1 }; };
export const q = (x, n = 2) => Math.round(x * 10 ** n) / 10 ** n;",
  "note": "Use the shaders and motion helpers verbatim. creature_template_js is the reference creature (uses Pen helpers: line, poly, ell, dot, stroke, shadedFill, inkRing, clip, curve, ellPts, mul, rad, thickAngle, INK): write a small Pen class with these, then design THIS story's creatures in the same way. Write everything else from the spec.",
  "creature_template_js": "const EMU = { body: "#4d3b2c", bodyDk: "#2f241b", streak: "#7a6048", neck: "#7f90ad", neckDk: "#56627c", head: "#3a2f28", beak: "#cdb68e", leg: "#8c8780", legDk: "#5e5a55" };
const ik2 = (h, f, L1, L2, back = -1) => { 
const dx = f[0] - h[0], dy = f[1] - h[1], d = Math.min(L1 + L2 - 1, Math.hypot(dx, dy));
const a = Math.atan2(dy, dx), c = Math.acos(Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, (L1 * L1 + d * d - L2 * L2) / (2 * L1 * d))));
const s = back < 0 ? 1 : -1; 
return [h[0] + Math.cos(a + s * c) * L1, h[1] + Math.sin(a + s * c) * L1];
};
export const emuSide = (p, opts = {}) => {
const { phase = 0, run = 0, peck = 0, blink = 0, expr = "calm", look = 0.3, seed = 1, tilt = 0, ruffle = 0 } = opts;
const g = p.g, two = Math.PI * 2, ow = 6;
const bob = run * 16 * Math.abs(Math.sin(two * phase)) + (1 - run) * 3 * Math.sin(seed * 3.1);
const lean = run * 0.16 + peck * 0.1 + tilt;
const hip = [292, 528 + bob * 0.6];
const bc = [290, 432 + bob], brx = 168, bry = 112;
const rot = (pt, c, a) => { const x = pt[0] - c[0], y = pt[1] - c[1]; return [c[0] + x * Math.cos(a) - y * Math.sin(a), c[1] + x * Math.sin(a) + y * Math.cos(a)]; };
const legs = [1, 0].map((k) => {
const ph = phase + k * 0.5, sx = Math.cos(two * ph), sy = Math.max(0, Math.sin(two * ph));
const h = [hip[0] + (k ? -14 : 14), hip[1]];
const foot = [h[0] + run * 135 * sx + (1 - run) * (k ? -22 : 26), 776 - run * 92 * sy];
const knee = ik2(h, foot, 138, 150, -1);
return { h, foot, knee, k, lift: sy * run };
});
const drawLeg = (L, far) => {
const col = far ? EMU.legDk : EMU.leg;
p.line([L.h, L.knee, L.foot], col, 15);
const fx = L.foot[0], fy = L.foot[1], ta = L.lift * 0.6;
for (const [dx, dy] of [[34, 2], [26, -6], [-14, 0]]) p.line([[fx, fy], [fx + dx * Math.cos(ta) - dy * Math.sin(ta), fy + dy * Math.cos(ta) + dx * Math.sin(ta) * 0.6]], col, 7);
p.dot(L.knee[0], L.knee[1], 9, col);
};
drawLeg(legs[0], true);
const nb = rot([392, 372 + bob], bc, -lean * 0.4);
let hd = [448 + run * 70, 128 + run * 72 + bob * 0.5];
hd = [hd[0] * (1 - peck) + 548 * peck, hd[1] * (1 - peck) + 712 * peck];
const nm = [ (nb[0] + hd[0]) / 2 + 30 - run * 10 + peck * 40, (nb[1] + hd[1]) / 2 + (peck ? -60 * peck : 10)];
const neckPts = curve(nb, nm, hd, 14);
p.line(neckPts, EMU.neck, 40);
for (let i = 2; i < 12; i++) { const [x, y] = neckPts[i]; p.stroke([[x - 6, y + 4], [x + 2, y - 4]], 3, EMU.neckDk); }
const bp = [];
for (let i = 0; i <= 64; i++) {
const a = Math.PI * 2 * i / 64, c = Math.cos(a), s = Math.sin(a);
let rx = brx, ry = bry;
if (c < -0.3) rx *= 1 + 0.12 * (-c - 0.3); 
let x = bc[0] + rx * c, y = bc[1] + ry * s + (c < 0 ? 26 * (-c) * (s > -0.2 ? 1 : 0.2) : 0);
if (s > 0.15) { const j = (i % 2 ? 1 : -0.4) * (16 + 6 * Math.sin(i * 1.7 + seed + ruffle)); y += j; } 
bp.push(rot([x, y], bc, -lean));
}
p.shadedFill(bp, EMU.body, EMU.bodyDk, rad(-110), brx, 0.4);
p.clip(bp, () => {
for (let i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
const x = bc[0] - 150 + ((i * 53 + seed * 31) % 300), y = bc[1] - 80 + ((i * 37) % 150);
p.stroke([[x, y], [x - 26, y + 22 + (i % 3) * 6]], 4, i % 2 ? EMU.streak : EMU.bodyDk);
}
});
p.inkRing(bp, ow, thickAngle(rad(-110)));
const th = rot([hip[0] + 12, hip[1] - 26], bc, -lean);
p.ell(th[0], th[1], 46, 40, EMU.body, ow);
for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) p.stroke([[th[0] - 30 + i * 14, th[1] + 18], [th[0] - 34 + i * 14, th[1] + 44]], 4, EMU.bodyDk);
